hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1424","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Yaman told us, Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Abbad bin Tamim told me, that his uncle was one of The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out with the people to the prayer place to draw water for them, so he stood up. So he called to stand, then he faced the Qiblah and wrapped around his cloak, so they were given water.” Abu Bakr said: There is no narration that I know of, “so give them water,” except in the narration of Shuaib bin Abi Hamza."
